From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] SystemServer: start UsbService for a device that is only a USB device

UsbService was started only when the device declares USB host or accessory
mode. PW3 has neither: its USB port is a device port (the ARC controller with
the kernel's Android gadget). Without UsbService there is no UsbDeviceManager,
which is what switches the gadget's functions (sys.usb.config), starts MTP,
shows the USB notification and its "File transfer" choice, and asks the user
to authorise a computer for adb (UsbDebuggingManager).

UsbService itself already creates its device manager exactly when
/sys/class/android_usb exists (the gadget is loaded before the framework
starts, docs/design/usb-mtp.md); SystemServer now starts it on the same
condition too.

--- a/services/java/com/android/server/SystemServer.java
+++ b/services/java/com/android/server/SystemServer.java
@@ -1249,9 +1249,14 @@
                     traceEnd();
                 }
 
+                // PW3: also for a device that is only a USB device, without host or
+                // accessory mode: the kernel's Android gadget (/sys/class/android_usb)
+                // is what UsbService's device manager drives (MTP, the USB notification,
+                // adb authorisation).
                 if (mPackageManager.hasSystemFeature(PackageManager.FEATURE_USB_HOST)
                         || mPackageManager.hasSystemFeature(
-                                PackageManager.FEATURE_USB_ACCESSORY)) {
+                                PackageManager.FEATURE_USB_ACCESSORY)
+                        || new File("/sys/class/android_usb").exists()) {
                     // Manage USB host and device support
                     traceBeginAndSlog("StartUsbService");
                     mSystemServiceManager.startService(USB_SERVICE_CLASS);
